course: dictionary
lesson: 4152
title: Gluten in bread
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Gluten is a protein found in wheat, barley and rye. A protein is a substance that living things need to grow and repair their bodies. In bread, gluten is what makes the dough stretchy.
explain: «Kneading pulls the dough's gluten proteins into long stretchy strands, like a net of tiny balloons.» Kneading means pushing and folding dough with your hands. The clue words are stretchy, strands and net: gluten is the stuff that holds the dough together so it can bend without tearing.
explain: «Yeast is a tiny fungus that eats sugar and makes bubbles of gas; stretchy gluten traps the gas so the dough rises.» The gluten works like a net that catches the gas, so the dough puffs up. Baking then kills the yeast and sets the holes, so the bread stays light.
explain: Gluten matters for some people's health. «People with coeliac disease get ill from gluten, so they eat gluten-free food.» Food labels must show whether gluten is in the food.
fact: Gluten is a protein found in wheat, barley and rye.
fact: Gluten makes dough stretchy, so bread can rise and become chewy.
fact: Coeliac disease (celiac in the US) makes people ill when they eat gluten.
fact: Gluten-free food is not healthier for most people.
fact: Gluten is uncountable, so you say some gluten, not a gluten.
exercise: «Kneading pulls the dough's gluten proteins into long stretchy strands.» What does kneading do to the gluten? | Freezes it solid | Turns it into gas | *Pulls it into long stretchy strands | Bakes it until crisp
exercise: Which grain does gluten come from? | *Wheat | Rice | Sugar | Potatoes
exercise: «Stretchy gluten traps the gas so the dough rises.» What does the gluten trap? | Light | *Gas bubbles made by yeast | Sugar crystals | Dust
test: Why does bread rise, according to «stretchy gluten traps the gas so the dough rises»? | Sugar goes hard in the oven | *Gluten traps gas bubbles made by yeast | Salt cools the dough down | Water freezes inside the dough
test: Someone with coeliac disease gets ill from which substance? | Salt | Sugar | Milk | *Gluten
exam: Why do people with coeliac disease eat gluten-free food? | Because gluten-free food is healthier for everyone | To get more gluten in their diet | Because it tastes better | *Because gluten makes them ill
